  "description": "LM-438: child-structure rules for the transaction validators (Java TransactionRules, Python transaction_rules, Rust validate_transaction, JS transaction_rules). Each case is a transaction tree in plain JSON, not proto JSON. A node has an optional uuid (absent: no uuid field; empty string: a uuid with empty raw_uuid), a transaction_type name and a security. A security is either {uuid, link: true}, which a pure validator treats as not cash, or {uuid, product_type} with an optional cash_details: true. Expected violations name the field path, the object_id (the UUID of the transaction that owns the children list) and the IDs the message must contain. as_of_seconds is set on every node by the Java golden-bytes test; the validators ignore it.",
